Source: xrdp-desktop-sessions
Section: net
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Dr. Christoph G. Keller <christoph.keller@gmx.net>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13)
Standards-Version: 4.7.0
Homepage: https://github.com/ckeller42/xrdp-nvidia-ppa
Vcs-Git: https://github.com/ckeller42/xrdp-nvidia-ppa.git
Vcs-Browser: https://github.com/ckeller42/xrdp-nvidia-ppa

Package: xrdp-nvidia-session
Architecture: all
Depends: xrdp (>= 0.10.80), xorgxrdp (>= 1:0.10.80), ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: pipewire-module-xrdp
Conflicts: thinky-remote-desktop
Replaces: thinky-remote-desktop
Description: run xrdp sessions on the NVIDIA GPU with NVENC encoding
 Detects an NVIDIA GPU at install time and configures xrdp so that every
 session runs Xorg on the NVIDIA driver (OpenGL/Vulkan on the GPU) and H.264
 is encoded by NVENC (xrdp-accel-assist). Without an NVIDIA driver nothing is
 changed. Re-run detection with: dpkg-reconfigure xrdp-nvidia-session

Package: xrdp-gnome-session
Architecture: all
Depends: xrdp (>= 0.10.80), ubuntu-session, gnome-shell, dconf-cli, adduser,
 yaru-theme-gtk, yaru-theme-icon, yaru-theme-gnome-shell, fonts-ubuntu,
 gnome-shell-extension-ubuntu-dock, gnome-shell-extension-appindicator, ubuntu-settings,
 ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: ubuntu-wallpapers, dmz-cursor-theme, xdg-desktop-portal-gnome, gnome-shell-extension-prefs,
 gnome-shell-extension-desktop-icons-ng, gnome-shell-extension-ubuntu-tiling-assistant,
 yaru-theme-sound, firefox, thunderbird, nautilus, gnome-terminal, gnome-text-editor, gnome-calculator,
 evince, eog, file-roller, rhythmbox, totem, shotwell, gnome-calendar, gnome-characters, gnome-clocks,
 gnome-weather, gnome-logs, gnome-system-monitor, gnome-disk-utility, baobab, seahorse, deja-dup,
 remmina, transmission-gtk, ubuntu-docs, yelp, libreoffice-writer, libreoffice-calc,
 libreoffice-impress, libreoffice-gnome, libreoffice-style-yaru, nautilus-sendto,
 gnome-software, flatpak, gnome-software-plugin-flatpak
Suggests: samba-common-bin, xrdp-nvidia-session
Conflicts: thinky-remote-desktop
Replaces: thinky-remote-desktop
Description: GNOME (Ubuntu session) desktop for xrdp users
 Makes GNOME with the Ubuntu look the default xrdp desktop (registered as
 x-session-manager; a user's own ~/.xsession still wins), with defaults for a
 remote/headless server: no screen lock, no
 blanking, no suspend, no animations. Provides add-remote-user, which creates
 a user with one password (also for Samba if installed). Adds Flathub if
 flatpak is installed.
